    <section class="white-box floor-plans-section" id="floor-plans" aria-labelledby="floor-plans-heading">
            <span class="section-label">Plans</span>
            <h2 class="section-title" id="floor-plans-heading">Eldeco Terra And Sol Floor Plans</h2>
            
                
                
<div class="description-content-box">
  <div class="desc-text"><p>Eldeco Terra And Sol's floor plan lineup is deliberately focused: two 3 BHK variants, both designed to minimize wasted circulation space and maximize usable living area.</p><h3>Configuration and Pricing</h3><div><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Unit </strong><strong>Type</strong></th><th><strong>Saleable Area</strong></th><th><strong>Price</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3 BHK Apartment</td><td>2150 Sq. Ft.</td><td>₹ 3.23 Cr</td></tr><tr><td>3 BHK Apartment</td><td>2450 Sq. Ft.</td><td>₹ 3.67 Cr</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3>Which of the Eldeco Terra and Sol floor plans is right for a first-time buyer?</h3><p>At this price point, Eldeco Terra And Sol isn't really an entry-level purchase, but the 3 BHK Apartment at 2150 Sq. Ft. for ₹ 3.23 Cr is the more accessible of the two variants. It carries full access to the 1.5-lakh-sq.-ft. clubhouse and the same low-density layout as the larger unit.</p><h3>Which Eldeco Terra and Sol unit should a rental investor choose?</h3><p>With only two unit sizes on offer, the smaller 2150 Sq. Ft.  variant is the more efficient pick for an investor on a per-sq.-ft. basis. New Gurgaon's proximity to Cyber City, Manesar Industrial Area, and Udyog Vihar supports rental demand from professionals working across these hubs.</p><h3>Is the Eldeco Terra And Sol 3 BHK a good choice for families?</h3><p>Yes. Both variants offer genuine 3 BHK room separation, and the project's low-density, privacy-focused layout, just 224 units total, means considerably less shared footfall than a denser Sector 80 development.</p><h3>Who should consider the larger Eldeco Terra and Sol unit?</h3><p>The 3 BHK Apartment  at 2450 Sq. Ft. for ₹ 3.67 Cr suits a buyer who wants the maximum space this project offers and plans to hold long-term. Before evaluating either floor plan, confirm the layout's natural light, ventilation, and outdoor-area privacy match the plan, since these details matter more in a low-density design than the raw square footage alone.</p><h3>What to verify before booking?</h3><ol><li>Confirm the RERA-filed carpet area against the saleable figure quoted for each unit</li><li>Check the construction-linked payment plan against the January 2031 possession date</li><li>Verify that stated room proportions match real-life furniture and layout needs before committing</li><li>Confirm outdoor living areas offer genuine privacy from neighbouring units, given the project's stated low-density design intent</li></ol></div>
  <div class="read-more-button-box">
    <button type="button" class="read-more-button global-read-more-btn" aria-expanded="false">Read More</button>
  </div>
</div>

            
