         their absence biases bounce rate and session counts in the flattering direction.
         On the way out we therefore load the SDK (in case the tab is only being switched) AND, if it
         has still not initialised, send one keepalive beacon ourselves.
         The stub deliberately does NOT classify traffic or build the full session — that logic stays
